course: dictionary
lesson: 12589
title: Disapprove: thinking something is wrong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To disapprove means to think that something or someone is bad or wrong. «Mum disapproves of muddy boots on the clean kitchen floor.» Mum does not like it, and she thinks it is wrong.
explain: You can show disapproval without saying a word. «Dad gave me a disapproving look when I stayed up past midnight.» The look shows he thinks it was wrong, even though he says nothing.
explain: Disapprove is often followed by of: you disapprove of something. «Grandma strongly disapproves of shouting at the dinner table.» Disapprove is a verb, so it changes: disapproves, disapproved, disapproving.
fact: Disapprove is a verb, so it can change: disapproves, disapproved, disapproving.
fact: «Disapprove» means to think that something or someone is bad or wrong.
fact: «A disapproving look» is a look that shows you think something is wrong, often without any words.
fact: A less common meaning is to refuse officially to agree to a plan or request. In that sense, people often use «reject» instead.
fact: The opposite of disapprove is approve, which means to think something is good or right.
exercise: «The teacher disapproves of running in the corridor.» What does disapproves mean here? | Is running in the corridor too | *Thinks running in the corridor is wrong | Runs faster than everyone else | Loves running in the corridor
exercise: «Her disapproving look made him put the cake back.» Which word tells you she thought taking the cake was wrong? | him | *disapproving | cake | made
exercise: Which word means the opposite of disapprove? | Forget | *Approve | Explain | Shout
test: «Dad disapproves of late nights on school days.» What does disapproves mean? | Likes sleeping in | *Thinks late nights are wrong | Thinks late nights are a good idea | Is tired of school
test: «My sister disapproved when I borrowed her pen without asking.» Was she pleased? | She gave me a present | She was pleased and smiled | *No, she thought it was wrong | She did not notice at all
exam: «The council disapproved the plan, so it could not go ahead.» What does disapproved mean here? | Painted it bright blue | Forgot all about it | Liked it very much | *Refused to agree to it officially
